<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{67AF1601-2ACB-0AE5-15B4-5B1155C92CB5}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="5" name="Content Placeholder 4"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{E8ADD891-6DA2-B6AD-1494-1A2F18EF4057}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph sz="half" idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="1447331" y="2010878"/><a:ext cx="4645152" cy="4566192"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr><a:normAutofit fontScale="70000" lnSpcReduction="20000"/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>The SIGA-CC1S Auto-Sync Output Module is an addressable module that is used to connect the following circuits: </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Audible and visible notification appliance circuits (synchronized or unsynchronized) </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Speaker circuits </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Two-way telephone communication circuits (three-state or four-state) </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>SIGA-CC1 DOES NOT PROVIDE SYNCHRONIZATION</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Upon command from the loop controller, the module connects the riser to the output circuit. The module requires one address on the signaling line circuit (SLC). Addresses are assigned electronically. There are no address switches. Diagnostic LEDs provide visible indication of the state of the module through the cover plate: </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Normal: Flashes green </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Alarm/active: Flashes red</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Title 2"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{71BC9AD9-2133-C70A-A145-6A5E0AB93A8B}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="title"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>SIGA-CC1(S)</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="6" name="Picture 5"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{2EB1ABD1-3CC5-345A-FFF2-8DFBBCC8B676}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId3"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="6722054" y="2579474"/><a:ext cx="4022615" cy="3429000"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Rectangle: Rounded Corners 3"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{33853021-1579-59B0-E404-FBB9B2A492FB}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="10228300" y="60641